<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
  ║  cr-dotnet-0010: Web.config Transformations — REMEDIATION APPLIED           ║
  ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

  This file (Web.Debug.config) previously contained build-time XDT transformation
  directives that modified Web.config values at compile time for the Debug build
  configuration. This approach is incompatible with cloud deployment pipelines
  where configuration must be externalized and runtime-configurable.

  REMEDIATION: Configuration has been externalized to environment variables and
  AWS Systems Manager (SSM) Parameter Store. Build-time transformations are no
  longer used. Configuration is injected at runtime, enabling immutable deployments.

  ── Environment Variables (AWS ECS / Elastic Beanstalk / App Runner) ──────────

  Set the following environment variables in your AWS deployment environment:

  DB_CONNECTION_STRING
    Description : Amazon RDS / RDS Proxy connection string
    Example     : Server=<rds-proxy-endpoint>;Database=tourdb;
                  User Id=<db-user>;Password=<db-password>;
    AWS Source  : AWS Secrets Manager secret or SSM SecureString parameter
                  /tour-management/db-connection-string

  AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME
    Description : S3 bucket name for tour image uploads
    Example     : my-tour-management-assets
    AWS Source  : SSM Parameter /tour-management/s3-bucket-name

  AWS_REGION
    Description : AWS region for SDK clients (S3, SSM, etc.)
    Example     : us-east-1
    AWS Source  : Set directly in task definition / environment

  ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT
    Description : Runtime environment name (Development / Staging / Production)
    Example     : Development  (for local debug)
    AWS Source  : Set directly in task definition / environment

  ── AWS Systems Manager Parameter Store ───────────────────────────────────────

  Parameters are stored under the path prefix /tour-management/:

    /tour-management/db-connection-string   (SecureString)
      → Replaces Web.config <connectionStrings> / Web.Debug.config XDT transforms

    /tour-management/s3-bucket-name         (String)
      → S3 bucket for tour image storage

  To enable SSM Parameter Store as a configuration source, add the
  Amazon.Extensions.Configuration.SystemsManager NuGet package and register
  the provider in Program.cs / Startup.cs:

    builder.Configuration.AddSystemsManager("/tour-management/");

  ── Local Development ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  For local development, set environment variables in launchSettings.json or
  use a .env file (never commit secrets to source control):

    "DB_CONNECTION_STRING": "Data Source=(LocalDB)\\MSSQLLocalDB;
        AttachDbFilename=|DataDirectory|\\tourdb.mdf;Integrated Security=True"

  ── Migration Notes ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The original XDT transformation in this file (line 5) was:
    <configuration xmlns:xdt="http://schemas.microsoft.com/XML-Document-Transform">
      <system.web>
        (empty — no active transformations were defined for Debug build)
      </system.web>
    </configuration>

  All environment-specific configuration previously managed through Web.config
  transformations is now handled at runtime via the priority chain:
    1. Environment variables  (highest priority)
    2. AWS SSM Parameter Store
    3. appsettings.json       (lowest priority / local dev fallback)
-->
